{
 "doc": "stages/filters.hag_delaunay.rst: 'If the non-ground point is within the trianulated area, the assigned ``HeightAboveGround`` is the difference between its ``Z`` value and a ground height interpolated from the three vertices of the containing triangle.' The ground is the plane z=x, so interpolation at (1.5,1.5) and (2.5,2.5) is exact: HAG 10 for both non-ground points.",
